PR #1291 — feat(payments-api): idempotent charges, cursor pagination, conditional invoice updates

Description (from PR body):
  - POST /v2/charges now honors `Idempotency-Key` (Stripe-style) so the mobile SDK can retry safely.
  - GET /v2/invoices switches from page-number to cursor pagination (newest first) — page
    numbers got slow past page 400 for our biggest merchants.
  - PATCH /v2/invoices/{id} supports `If-Match` for optimistic concurrency. The body is JSON
    Merge Patch (RFC 7396), per our public API guidelines.
  - Invoice `status` gains `partially_paid` for split payments.
  v2 is our public API; ~200 merchants integrate against it (plus our iOS/Android SDKs).
  Tests: added happy-path tests for each endpoint; all green.

